local.properties

# Release signing - the key and its passwords never go to the repo.
# CI reads the same values from SIGNING_* secrets instead.
/keystore.properties
*.jks
*.keystore

# The README on GitHub is written by hand; this local copy is not the source of truth.
/README.md

# The handoff notes are for whoever picks this up next, not for the repo's readers. Kept
# locally and deliberately untracked - it names the phone, the test device's build, and a
# running list of what is broken.
/HANDOFF.md

# The release-notes draft, fed to `git tag -F`. Local only, like HANDOFF.md; the tag message
# is what actually publishes the notes, so this file must never be committed.
/日志.txt

# The agent's per-session memory - the same category as HANDOFF.md: running notes on what
# was tried, device quirks, and round-by-round debugging history. For whoever (whatever)
# picks this up next, not for the repo's readers.
/.workbuddy/
